            <div xml:id="d146">

                <pb facs="0338" n="224" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg224"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">150.01/802</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Norwegian Minister</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bryn</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-19"><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                        1924</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note dated February 20, 1924, with respect to certain provisions of the
                    new immigration bill (H. R. 6540) introduced in the House of Representatives on
                    February 1, 1924.</p>
                <p>You may be assured that all questions relating to the appropriate recognition of
                    the treaty provisions to which you refer are having proper consideration.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles E. Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
